{"ticker":"COROMANDEL","symbol":"COROMANDEL","instrumentId":3022857,"name":"Coromandel Intl.","industry":"NSE-Chemicals-Agricultural","about":"Coromandel International Ltd., a flagship company of the Murugappa Group, is India’s pioneer and leading agri-solutions provider. the country’s first fertilizer plant in Ranipet, Tamil Nadu, Coromandel has evolved into the largest private sector phosphatic fertilizer company in India. It is also the world’s largest neem-based bio-pesticide manufacturer and the leading organic fertilizer marketer in India. The company operates across two major segments: Nutrients and Crop Protection, offering a diverse range of products including fertilizers, bio-pesticides, specialty nutrients, and organic fertilizers. Coromandel supports over 3 million farmers through its 750+ Gromor retail outlets, providing comprehensive farm solutions and advisory services. With 18 manufacturing facilities and strong R&D capabilities, Coromandel is recognized for its commitment to sustainability and innovation.","website":"www.coromandel.biz","location":"Secunderabad, INDIA","exchange":"NSE","fetchedAt":"2026-11-20T13:13:56.101Z","basis":"consolidated","price":{"value":1972,"changePct":0.6636038795303726,"week52High":2425,"week52Low":1673.7},"stats":[{"label":"Market capitalization","value":"₹58,186 Cr"},{"label":"Sales","value":"₹33,242 Cr"},{"label":"Shares in float","value":"129,826,000"},{"label":"No. of funds","value":"599"},{"label":"Shares held by funds","value":"93,871,540"},{"label":"Dividend yield","value":"0.56%"},{"label":"Book value","value":"4.63"},{"label":"U/D vol ratio","value":"1.5"},{"label":"LTDebt / equity","value":"1.0%"},{"label":"Alpha","value":"-0.04"},{"label":"Beta","value":"1.07"},{"label":"EPS growth rate","value":"5%"},{"label":"P/E ratio","value":"37.21"},{"label":"5-year P/E range","value":"13–40"},{"label":"Return on equity","value":"15.6%"},{"label":"Cash flow (INR)","value":"52.8"},{"label":"Volume","value":"351,342"},{"